tton/Shift/Continue/","source-block-115","In Sequencer mode, hold Shift and press Play to resume a stopped sequence from where it stopped.",["Continue"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/1-Left/7-Play-Button/Shift/Continue/","source-block-215","Source",["Continue"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/1-Left/7-Play-Button/Shift/Continue/","source-block-228","Launchpad/UG/04 Launchpad Pro Interface/02 Shift",["Continue","Source"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/1-Left/7-Play-Button/Shift/Continue/","source-block-285","Launchpad/UG/09 Sequencer/02 Steps View/05 Playback",["Continue","Source"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/1-Left/8-Record-Button/","source-block-80","Record button",[]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/1-Left/8-Record-Button/","source-block-98","In Session mode, Record overdubs the playing clip on an armed track. While a clip records, press Record to end the recording; the clip flashes red until it stops.",["Record button"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/1-Left/8-Record-Button/","source-block-264","In Sequencer mode, press Record to turn on live recording; the button lights red. Notes played in the Play Area, and MIDI arriving over USB or MIDI In, are recorded while the sequencer plays.",["Record button"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/1-Left/8-Record-Button/","source-block-459","Gestures",["Record button"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/1-Left/8-Record-Button/","source-block-474","Launchpad/UI/Area/1-Left/8-Record-Button/Shift/Capture-MIDI",["Record button","Gestures"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/1-Left/8-Record-Button/","source-block-542","Remote control",["Record button"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/1-Left/8-Record-Button/","source-block-563","Programmer mode: CC 10",["Record button","Remote control"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/1-Left/8-Record-Button/","source-block-590","Source",["Record button"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/1-Left/8-Record-Button/","source-block-603","Launchpad/UG/05 Session Mode/01 Ableton Live Session View",["Record button","Source"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/1-Left/8-Record-Button/","source-block-669","Launchpad/UG/05 Session Mode/05 Record Arm and Recording",["Record button","Source"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/1-Left/8-Record-Button/","source-block-734","Launchpad/UG/09 Sequencer/02 Steps View/06 Record",["Record button","Source"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/1-Left/8-Record-Button/Shift/Capture-MIDI/","source-block-104","Capture MIDI",[]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/1-Left/8-Record-Button/Shift/Capture-MIDI/","source-block-121","In Session mode, hold Shift and press Record to run Live's Capture MIDI. It puts the notes recently played on armed or input-monitored tracks into a new clip, or overdubs them onto the playing clip.",["Capture MIDI"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/1-Left/8-Record-Button/Shift/Capture-MIDI/","source-block-323","Source",["Capture MIDI"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/1-Left/8-Record-Button/Shift/Capture-MIDI/","source-block-336","Launchpad/UG/05 Session Mode/01 Ableton Live Session View",["Capture MIDI","Source"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/","source-block-65","Grid",[]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/","source-block-74","The 8 × 8 grid of 64 pads. It plays notes, launches clips or edits sequences, depending on the mode.",["Grid"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/","source-block-179","Controls",["Grid"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/","source-block-194","Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/Pad",["Grid","Controls"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/","source-block-231","Source",["Grid"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/","source-block-244","Launchpad/UG/03 Hardware Overview",["Grid","Source"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/Pad/","source-block-80","Pad",[]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/Pad/","source-block-88","The grid's 64 pads sense velocity and pressure and light in color. What a pad does depends on the mode.",["Pad"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/Pad/","source-block-195","Launchpad/UI/Mode/1-Session: launches the clip in its slot of Ableton Live's Session View. In the Volume, Pan, Sends and Device views, a row or column of pads is a fader.",["Pad"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/Pad/","source-block-373","Launchpad/UI/Mode/2-Note: plays a note in the Chromatic or Scale layout, or a Drum Rack slot when the armed Live track holds a Drum Rack.",["Pad"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/Pad/","source-block-518","Launchpad/UI/Mode/3-Chord: plays a scale note in the Note Area, a triad in the orange column, or a stored chord in the white Chord Bank.",["Pad"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/Pad/","source-block-662","Launchpad/UI/Mode/4-Custom: sends the MIDI note, control change or Program Change that the Custom Mode assigns to it. A whole row or column can be a fader.",["Pad"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/Pad/","source-block-825","Launchpad/UI/Mode/5-Sequencer: in Steps View, a pad in the top half is one of the Pattern's 32 steps, and a pad in the bottom half plays a note in the Play Area.",["Pad"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/Pad/","source-block-994","Remote control",["Pad"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/Pad/","source-block-1015","Programmer mode: notes 11–88. A pad sends note 10 × row + column, with rows and columns counted 1 to 8 from the bottom left, so the bottom row sends 11–18 and the top row 81–88.",["Pad","Remote control"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/Pad/","source-block-1204","Source",["Pad"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/Pad/","source-block-1217","Launchpad/UG/01 Introduction",["Pad","Source"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/Pad/","source-block-1254","Launchpad/UG/05 Session Mode/01 Ableton Live Session View",["Pad","Source"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/Pad/","source-block-1320","Launchpad/UG/05 Session Mode/04 Track Controls/09 Fader Orientation",["Pad","Source"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/Pad/","source-block-1396","Launchpad/UG/06 Note Mode",["Pad","Source"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/Pad/","source-block-1430","Launchpad/UG/07 Chord Mode/01 Overview",["Pad","Source"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/Pad/","source-block-1477","Launchpad/UG/08 Custom Modes/04 Set Up a Custom Mode",["Pad","Source"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/Pad/","source-block-1538","Launchpad/UG/09 Sequencer/02 Steps View",["Pad","Source"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/2-Grid/Pad/","source-block-1586","Launchpad/PRG/05 Software Integration/11 Programmer Layout",["Pad","Source"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/3-Right/","source-block-65","Right column",[]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/3-Right/","source-block-82","The eight buttons down the right edge of the grid, one beside each row. They launch scenes in Session mode. In Sequencer mode they open the sequencer's views, and the bottom one prints a Pattern to an Ableton Live clip.",["Right column"]],["Launchpad/UI/Area/3-Right/","source-block-305","With Launchpad/UI/Area/4-Bottom/0-Setup-Button held, the green button in this column chooses Live mode and the orange button at the bottom chooses Programmer mode.",["Right column"]]],"format_version":5}